   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package initializer for the exllamav3 library. It runs whenever the package is imported, and its main job is to set up the environment correctly before anything else happens. Specifically, it disables a ROCm profiler registration hook that would otherwise leave a CPU thread spinning, ensures PyTorch is installed (raising a helpful error with install instructions if it isn't), and configures sensible defaults such as enabling expandable segments for the CUDA caching allocator and pointing Triton at its AMD backend on ROCm systems. Finally, it imports and exposes the library's main public API \u2014 including `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `Cache`, and the various generator and sampler classes \u2014 so users can access them directly from the top-level `exllamav3` namespace."
  },
