   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "0ea8643af9a50c6fe4c69a1118b07fb480ef6b33a8c7754071ee824411f184df",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package initializer for the exllamav3 library. It runs before any other module in the package is imported, and its main job is to set up the environment correctly before PyTorch gets loaded. Specifically, it disables the ROCm profiler registration hook (to avoid a spinning HSA event thread wasting a CPU core), applies sensible default CUDA allocator settings (expandable segments, unless the user has configured their own allocator or is on Windows/ROCm), and points Triton at its AMD backend on ROCm systems where both backends might otherwise conflict. After these environment tweaks, it imports torch (raising a helpful error if it's missing, since exllamav3 intentionally doesn't pin a torch version) and then exposes the library's public API \u2014 `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `Cache`, `Generator`, sampler components, and so on \u2014 so users can simply `import exllamav3` and access everything."
  }
